WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.030
(residents shouting in Mandarin)

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:03.630
- [Reporter] Residents
in China's financial hubs

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:05.088
say they're going hungry.

00:00:05.088 --> 00:00:09.171
(residents shouting in Mandarin)

00:00:10.212 --> 00:00:13.310
(speaker speaking in Mandarin)

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:15.410
Many people have been
unable to leave their homes

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:17.186
to buy food since late March.

00:00:17.186 --> 00:00:21.103
(speaker speaking in Mandarin)

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.700
That's because Shanghai officials
began a citywide lockdown

00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:30.839
to tame the country's
biggest COVID-19 outbreak

00:00:30.839 --> 00:00:32.503
in the past two years.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:37.073
Some residents have also taken
to social media to complain.

00:00:38.330 --> 00:00:41.220
- It has prompted a lot of
people in Shanghai to ask

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:42.630
is this the right policy?

00:00:42.630 --> 00:00:46.480
Is the cost of this lockdown too great?

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:47.690
- [Reporter] As authorities try to tame

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:49.670
the fast spreading Omicron variant,

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:51.750
the growing public
discontent could challenge

00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:54.893
Beijing's commitment to its
dynamic zero-COVID policy.

00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:59.110
Shanghai officials have
acknowledged its strategy

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:01.580
of lockdowns, mass tests and quarantines

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:03.920
has made it difficult for
tens of thousands of families

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:05.240
to secure food.

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:06.680
So, they've rolled out a massive effort

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:08.083
to deliver necessities.

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:10.940
Local officials said there were

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:13.360
around 11,000 couriers on the job

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:16.935
and delivery companies had
about 100,000 other workers.

00:01:16.935 --> 00:01:18.380
(plastic rustling)

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:20.390
Volunteers have also
been going door to door

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:23.280
to deliver other supplies
including medicine.

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:26.240
Plus people from across the
country have been pitching in

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:28.080
including from as far as Xinjiang,

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:30.730
where workers package bread for residents.

00:01:30.730 --> 00:01:31.970
There's also fresh vegetables

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:34.680
coming from Shanghai's
neighboring province.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:35.900
But some residents have said

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:38.380
that they're not getting enough
food from these deliveries.

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:40.480
- There are some people who are doing okay

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:43.020
but there's also unquestionably
people who are are living

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:46.290
on basically the barest minimum of food

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:49.400
with no protein and very
little in terms of quantity.

00:01:49.400 --> 00:01:50.233
- [Reporter] For instance,

00:01:50.233 --> 00:01:51.910
a family of two received this package

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:54.430
from the government on the
second day of the lockdown.

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:55.300
The father and daughter

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:57.920
said it was all consumed
in about four days

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:01.120
and the next delivery came
about two weeks later.

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.050
So to feed themselves,

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:04.300
some people are getting
up as early as 6:00 am

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:06.750
to place an order on
grocery delivery apps.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:09.068
At a time when supplies are
more likely to be available.

00:02:09.068 --> 00:02:10.319
(massager rumbling)

00:02:10.319 --> 00:02:12.570
(speaker speaking in Mandarin)

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:15.080
- This man's wife recorded
him using a massage gun

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:16.840
to help him more quickly
hit the pay button

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:18.923
to get his order through before others.

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:24.367
Some residents have teamed up
with neighbors to buy in bulk.

00:02:24.367 --> 00:02:27.269
- We've got over 150 parcels in here.

00:02:27.269 --> 00:02:30.070
We ordered for the whole building again.

00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:32.224
- Or they're bartering with each other.

00:02:32.224 --> 00:02:34.480
(speaker speaking in Mandarin)

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:36.160
The struggle to get food has sparked anger

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:37.791
in some communities.

00:02:37.791 --> 00:02:41.874
(residents shouting in Mandarin)

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.480
This video was posted on Weibo,

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:48.020
China's equivalent of Twitter,

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:49.650
and it was later taken down.

00:02:49.650 --> 00:02:52.534
It shows local police trying
to contain a crowd of people.

00:02:52.534 --> 00:02:55.830
(residents shouting in Mandarin)

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:58.523
Weibo didn't respond to
a request for comment.

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:01.210
These food shortages have largely stemmed

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:03.270
from the city's strict COVID restrictions

00:03:03.270 --> 00:03:04.830
which have confined many of the city's

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:06.610
food delivery workers at home.

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:09.510
And some have chosen not to
work for fear of getting sick.

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:12.460
Also for new supplies to enter the city,

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:14.640
truck drivers need to test negative.

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:15.740
- Once you come into the city

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:17.413
and you've delivered your
supplies, it's not clear

00:03:17.413 --> 00:03:20.340
if you can necessarily get
into the neighboring province

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:22.480
to be able to pick up
another run of supplies

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:26.240
because the authorities
won't necessarily allow you

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:28.190
into the province because you've just come

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:30.420
from a high risk zone.

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:32.642
- Shanghai officials have
pledged to do better.

00:03:32.642 --> 00:03:36.559
(speaker speaking in Mandarin)

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:39.340
- [Reporter] However, the anxiety

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:41.040
of not having enough to eat is raising

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.130
some collective memories
from China's famine

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:44.786
about five decades ago.

00:03:44.786 --> 00:03:48.200
- China's modern history
has had a lot of instances

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:52.890
of deprivation and of quite
serious lack of access to food.

00:03:52.890 --> 00:03:54.810
This is a 21st century twist on that

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:56.310
but it has reminded people

00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:59.420
of the importance of having stockpiles.

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:00.800
- [Reporter] And the situation in Shanghai

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:01.870
has prompted some people

00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:04.330
in other cities to prepare for the worst.

00:04:04.330 --> 00:04:05.627
On Weibo the topic,

00:04:05.627 --> 00:04:08.810
"What to prepare if I suddenly
receive a quarantine notice?"

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:11.850
has attracted more than 200 million views.

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:14.520
And Chinese state media
published this diagram

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.500
which outlines the items
you need to prepare

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:18.373
to stay at a quarantine center.

00:04:19.850 --> 00:04:21.560
Even though Shanghai officials announced

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:24.410
that they have lifted some
measures despite record cases,

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:26.440
people have started to
question more than just

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:28.804
the government's handling
of the food shortage.

00:04:28.804 --> 00:04:32.721
(speaker speaking in Mandarin)

00:04:36.499 --> 00:04:39.220
- There is a great
degree of dissatisfaction

00:04:39.220 --> 00:04:41.300
about whether or not it's the wisest way

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.030
to deal with this challenge.

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:45.530
This dynamic zero- COVID policy

00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:48.660
of really just trying
to eradicate the virus

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:51.030
every time they see it
anywhere within China.

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:53.290
If it ends up overwhelming Shanghai,

00:04:53.290 --> 00:04:57.130
it's going to challenge that
idea that China's government

00:04:57.130 --> 00:04:59.002
has been more successful
than the rest of the world

00:04:59.002 --> 00:05:00.437
at containing COVID.

00:05:00.437 --> 00:05:01.820
- [Reporter] But the
experience in Shanghai

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:04.260
hasn't prompted any
indication from Beijing

00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:06.840
that it's ready to rethink
its COVID strategy.

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:09.130
The head of China's
COVID-19 Response Task Force

00:05:09.130 --> 00:05:12.160
said its dynamic zero
COVID policy was scientific

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:14.720
and would bring maximum results.

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:17.030
So, with little sign that
Beijing is willing to adjust

00:05:17.030 --> 00:05:18.370
its pandemic strategy,

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:20.593
some residents have
taken to their balconies.

00:05:20.593 --> 00:05:23.690
(residents shouting in Mandarin)

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:26.690
To shout encouragement and hope
that the lockdown ends soon.

